---
title: Pancakes
servings: 2
tags: [vegetarian, quick, weekend]
time: 25 minutes
source: Adapted from Easy Pancakes in cooklang/cookcli (MIT), https://github.com/cooklang/cookcli/blob/main/seed/Breakfast/Easy%20Pancakes.cook
---

Blend the @eggs{3}, @all-purpose flour{125%g}, @whole milk{250%ml} and a pinch
of @sea salt{} in a #blender{} until smooth.

Pour into a bowl and let it rest ~{15%minutes}.

Melt a little @unsalted butter{} in a #large non-stick frying pan{} over medium
heat, tilting the pan to coat it.

Pour in a ladle of batter and tilt so it covers the base thinly. Cook
~{1%minute} to 2 minutes, until golden underneath and coming away at the edges.

Flip and cook ~{1%minute} more. Serve straight away with whatever you like on
top.

> These are thin pancakes, close to crepes. Butter the pan again every few.
